them and modified files say so.

The text that travels is licenses/Apache-2.0.txt, and it is the canonical
Apache-2.0 as published at https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0.txt
(sha256 cfc7749b…, checked 2026-08-11) — not Waveshare's copy of it. The two
differ only in the appendix, the "how to apply the License to your work"
boilerplate, which Waveshare filled in with their own copyright line and which
is not part of the license terms. The canonical text is used because this same
file is what §4 relies on for the Noto Emoji artwork, and a file stamped with
one copyright holder's name should not be the thing another holder's grant
points at. Sections 1-9 are identical either way, and the URL the license
itself names is the one this file came from. (Contrast
licenses/BSD-3-Clause.txt and licenses/OFL-1.1.txt, which ARE verbatim upstream
copies — see §3 and §4. There the upstream file itself is the artifact worth
