Upstream ships a LICENSE but no NOTICE file, so §4(d) adds nothing to carry
over here (checked 2026-08-08).

All 35 files under vendor/, plus boards/waveshare_rp2350_touch_lcd_2.8c.h and
pico_sdk_import.cmake, were compared against upstream file by file (37 in
total — upstream's own LICENSE is not among them, and is not vendored: see the
paragraph above): 30 are byte-identical to it after line-ending normalization,
and the modified ones are exactly the seven listed below. Each carries a notice
at the top of the file, per §4(b):

  - vendor/bsp/bsp_gt911.c
      * g_gt911_irq_flag marked volatile — written in the GPIO IRQ callback,
        read in the main loop.
      * read buffer zero-initialized — an uninitialized buffer let a failed
        I2C read present a stale data-ready bit. Touch is an exercised path.
      * product-id buffer widened to data[5]={0} so the 4-byte read is
        NUL-terminated before strstr()/printf("%s") (stack over-read).
  - vendor/bsp/bsp_gt911.h
      * exported bsp_gt911_reset() and bsp_gt911_reg_read_byte() so the
        application can re-initialize a misbehaving GT911 with a bounded retry
        (bsp_gt911_init() retries forever and would hang the main loop).
  - vendor/bsp/bsp_st7701s.h
      * BSP_LCD_PCLK_FREQ lowered 16 MHz -> 10 MHz, dropping the refresh from
        ~60 Hz to ~38 Hz so the ~19 ms procedural face render fits inside one
        scan period (tear-free). Expressions are slow, so the lower rate is fine.
  - vendor/bsp/pio_rgb.c
      * two manual pixel-copy loops replaced with memcpy (the DMA-complete ISR
        copy and the framebuffer blit). Both run every frame.
  - vendor/bsp/CMakeLists.txt
      * dropped the no-OS-FatFS-SD link; comments trimmed.
  - vendor/CMakeLists.txt
      * dropped the lvgl and no-OS-FatFS-SD add_subdirectory lines; the face
        firmware uses neither.
  - boards/waveshare_rp2350_touch_lcd_2.8c.h  (Raspberry Pi BSD-3, see §3)
      * PICO_PLATFORM set via comment-form for pico-sdk 2.1.1 compatibility.
      * PICO_FLASH_SIZE_BYTES default raised 4 MB -> 16 MB to match the board
        actually shipped; the #define below it already assumed 16 MB.

Not vendored from upstream:

  - bsp_sd_card.* and the no-OS-FatFS-SD dependency — the face firmware does
    not use the microSD slot.
  - lvgl — not used by the face firmware.
  - The wiki's schematic PDF is not redistributed here: it is not part of the
    Apache-2.0 repository. See README.md for the official link.

Known upstream issue worked around at the call site (not patched here, so the
vendored file stays identical to upstream):

  - GUI_Paint.c Paint_DrawString_EN swaps foreground and background before
    handing them to Paint_DrawChar. Every src/face_serial.c call compensates by
    passing the arguments as (background, foreground); the reason is spelled out
    once, at the first call site in draw_confirm(). Patching the vendored file
    instead would silently break all of those calls.

Known upstream issues left as-is (not exercised by the face firmware, kept
faithful so upstream diffs stay readable):

  - bsp_battery.c average_filter: uninitialized accumulator + per-element
    division. The battery module is not called by face_serial.
  - bsp_qmi8658.c: double-precision sqrt/atan (IMU module, not used yet).
  - bsp_pcf85063.c: unused local (RTC module, not used).
  - GUI_Paint.c (Scale==2 path): `Color&0xff == BLACK` operator-precedence bug.
    face_serial draws with native scale65, not the 1bpp path.
  - GUI_Paint.c Paint_DrawNum: the digit buffer can be overrun by a
    sufficiently long number. face_serial does not call it.


